"
`;

exports[`git.grove.wake.tailnet given: [case2] an ec2 grove whose row is an ssm-era relic, box up when: [t2] it is woken and ssh does not answer then: the failure reads as a snapshot 1`] = `
"      ├─ 💥 no ssh answer from camper@grove-sandpine-v20260901:22 within 0s

  ssh said:
    ssh: connect to host grove-sandpine-v20260901 port 22: Connection timed out

  first, is THIS machine on the tailnet? a caller off it reaches no grove —
    check the tailnet — tailscale status (is this machine a peer?), then tailscale ping grove-sandpine-v20260901
  a grove rebuilt joins the tailnet under a new \`-N\` suffix, and shows in that list;
  pin the live name as the row's host —
    git grove set grove-sandpine-v20260901 --at camper@<tailnet-host>:22

  the box answers ec2, but not ssh. TWO causes, and their cures are
  OPPOSITE — tell them apart before you act:

  (a) it needs longer. a box resumed from hibernate must rejoin the
      tailnet before its ssh answers, and that can outlast --timeout
      fix: wake it again — a wake is idempotent
        rhx git.grove.wake grove-sandpine-v20260901

  (b) 🔴 it is STARVED. a box thrashed under load cannot answer a handshake,
      so a second wake cures NAUGHT, and each one costs another 0s
      tell: git.grove.list reads 🔴 MUTE — the port accepts, yet no ssh
            banner comes back — rather than 🔴 DOWN, and saturation
            reads a full run queue
        rhx git.grove.list
        rhx git.grove.saturation grove-sandpine-v20260901
      fix: the lever is LOAD — fell or stop crews, or provision more box.
           🟡 neither is reachable while it is mute, so this is a
           PROVISION decision for a human
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.wake.tailnet given: [case3] an ec2 grove, and the keyrack will not hand over credentials when: [t0] it is woken then: the power failure reads as a snapshot 1`] = `
"🔐 keyrack: AWS_PROFILE is locked 🔒 — rhx keyrack unlock
   └─ ✋ the rack did not hand over AWS_PROFILE for env=camp

  fix: the rack named it above — read that line, not this one.
       locked 🔒 wants an unlock; absent 🫧 wants a set, and a
       set overwrites a live value, so read it before you type.
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.wake.tailnet given: [case4] a grove whose row is not json when: [t0] it is woken then: the halt reads as a snapshot, the temp forest masked 1`] = `
"✋ ConstraintError: grove row unreadable — not json
   ├─ row: $FOREST/groves/grove-sandpine-corrupt.json
   └─ fix: re-register it — git grove set <grove> --at camper@<tailnet-host>:22
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.wake.tailnet given: [case5] a grove that is not registered when: [t0] it is woken then: the hint reads as a snapshot 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude — grove 'grove-sandpine-unregistered' is not registered

  fix: register it in the shape of its box —
    a grove with no aws instance (hetzner, any box that never sleeps):
      git grove set grove-sandpine-unregistered --at camper@<tailnet-host>:22
    an ec2 grove, which aws powers up:
      git grove set grove-sandpine-unregistered --exid grove-sandpine-unregistered --env camp --account <id>
    ⚠️ an account on a non-aws box sends the wake to hunt an ec2 that is not there
  or list what is registered —
    rhx git.grove.list
"
`;
